invariant: INV-16
file: poly1305.c
catches: test/widemul-builds.sh
reason: poly1305.c guards its call to the vector path on a macro no
  build defines, so a host object's native copy runs the portable loop
  for a session with the multiply bit. Nothing else objects:
  poly1305_vector.c still compiles and links, bin/poly1305_equiv_test
  calls it directly, and every vector and Wycheproof case passes, because
  the portable loop computes the same tags; only the time is wrong. The
  script compiles poly1305_native.c as a host object does and requires
  its object to call poly1305_vector_blocks_native.

--- old
#ifdef CH_POLY1305_VECTOR
    if (n >= POLY1305_VECTOR_MIN) {
--- new
#ifdef CH_POLY1305_VECTOR_PATH
    if (n >= POLY1305_VECTOR_MIN) {
